### Area 4: the role-permission matrix, masking and the rules for data sent to AI.
### Sign in first (requests/auth.http), then paste the op_csrf cookie value below.
### Reading the matrix needs roles.read; changing it needs roles.manage (SYSTEM_ADMIN
### holds both, AUDITOR holds roles.read). Any other role gets 403 FORBIDDEN with a
### traceId, and the refusal is audited.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@csrf = paste the op_csrf cookie value here after signing in

### Every role with its permissions and data scope, the permissions in display order,
### and the cells that cannot change (the system admin never approves, posts or pays).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/matrix

### Grant or revoke one permission. Audited. Granting twice changes and audits nothing.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/matrix/FINANCE/permissions/orders.read
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "granted": true }

### A locked cell: the system admin cannot be given payments.post. Answers 409.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/matrix/SYSTEM_ADMIN/permissions/payments.post
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "granted": true }

### Which records a role may see: all, brands or own. Stored and shown; not enforced yet.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/matrix/PRODUCT_MANAGER/data-scope
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "dataScope": "brands" }

### Make one role hold exactly what another holds, with its data scope.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/matrix/copy
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "fromRole": "FINANCE", "toRole": "LOGISTICS" }

### Synthetic customers with the sample masking rule applied for YOUR role.
### Sign in as WAREHOUSE and the note comes back as null, with the reason.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/masking/sample

### What data may go to which AI provider. The default is synthetic data only.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/ai-destinations

### Ask about one request, as the AI gateway will. Real data is refused with a reason.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/governance/ai-destinations/check
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrf}}

{ "provider": "bedrock", "classification": "internal", "origin": "real" }
